BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9e8cc66330853af02800175c
SUMMARY:The Rock Orchestra by Candlelight
DTSTAMP:20260926T080420Z
DTSTART:20261119T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:After mesmerizing audiences across Europe and the UK\, The Rock
	 Orchestra by Candlelight is set to electrify the USA once again. Prepare 
	for a spellbinding spectacle that infuses iconic rock and metal anthems wi
	th a hauntingly beautiful energy. In an ethereal candlelit setting\, this 
	band of fourteen classical musicians unleashes effortlessly enchanting mel
	odies alongside powerful walls of distortion. Witness the unexpected union
	 of classical music and metal. The UK-based ensemble is a rotating collect
	ive of some of the world’s most talented musicians and vocalists who reima
	gine the music of beloved rock bands\, including Metallica\, AC/DC\, Rolli
	ng Stones\, Rage Against the Machine\, My Chemical Romance\, Linkin' Park\
	, System of a Down\, Guns N' Roses\, Evanescence\, Papa Roach\, The Cranbe
	rries\, and more!\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/the-rock
	-orchestra-by-candlelight
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/the-rock-orchestra-by-cand
	lelight
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Concerts
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9c02a03ef03ee122f25d86b2
SUMMARY:Happy Holidays with the Mighty Wurlitzer
DTSTAMP:20260926T080420Z
DTSTART:20261205T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Friends of Music Hall\, Happy Holidays with the Mi
	ghty Wurlitzer returns with an enchanting The Night Before Christmas-theme
	d concert. Step into the magic and nostalgia of the holidays and let this 
	musical celebration become part of your family's annual tradition. This sp
	ectacular evening brings together an exceptional lineup of talent\, anchor
	ed by featured organist Richie Gregory. Introduced to the theatre pipe org
	an at age one\, this accomplished musician is a two-time competitor in the
	 ATOS Young Theatre Organist Competition and serves as Associate Organist 
	at the Ohio Theatre. Adding a dynamic visual rhythm to the night\, (CA)² x
	 Soul Syndicate will present a choreographic blend of Hip Hop Street dance
	 and Contemporary movement\, delivering intricate floor work and vivid sto
	rytelling set to classic holiday songs. The musical celebration continues 
	with the Music Hall Holiday Chorus under the direction of Jason Alexander 
	Holmes\, Associate Director of Choruses of the May Festival. This festive 
	ensemble unites local community and church choirs with professional singer
	s for a joyful\, harmonious sound reflecting the very spirit of Cincinnati
	. Guiding audiences through this evening of community\, dance\, and song i
	s returning emcee Kyle Inskeep\, the popular WKRC news anchor who brings h
	is signature warmth\, wit\, and cheer to the Music Hall stage. Join us for
	 an unforgettable night.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/h
	appy-holidays-with-the-mighty-wurlitzer-26
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/happy-holidays-with-the-mi
	ghty-wurlitzer-26
LOCATION:Music Hall Ballroom\, Music Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Concerts
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4b07c85508cf345756ffdcdf
SUMMARY:Rocky Mountain High Experience®: John Denver Christmas
DTSTAMP:20260926T080420Z
DTSTART:20261218T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to fall in love with the holidays all over again! Roc
	ky Mountain High Experience®: A John Denver Christmas takes you back to th
	e 1970s\, a golden era when John Denver's music lit up the airwaves and wa
	rmed hearts across America. Acclaimed performer Rick Schuler brings it all
	 back to life in a holiday concert you'll be talking about long after the 
	season ends. Sing along to the Denver classics you know by heart: "Rocky M
	ountain High\," "Take Me Home\, Country Roads\," "Annie's Song\," and "Sun
	shine on My Shoulders." Then comes the holiday magic as the evening pays l
	oving tribute to Denver's legendary Christmas specials with seasonal treas
	ures like "Aspenglow\," "Silent Night\," "Joy to the World\," and "Chestnu
	ts Roasting on an Open Fire" - the perfect soundtrack to the most wonderfu
	l time of the year. Lifelong superfan or first-time listener\, it doesn't 
	matter. You'll walk out inspired\, uplifted\, and full of holiday cheer. T
	his is a celebration for all ages and one show this season you won't want 
	to miss. Come experience the magic of John Denver\, live!\n\nhttps://www.c
	incinnatiarts.org/events/detail/rocky-mountain-high-experience-john-denver
	-christmas-26
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/rocky-mountain-high-experi
	ence-john-denver-christmas-26
LOCATION:Jarson-Kaplan Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Concerts
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
